,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":651.2186017,"data":"Third, (a + 3)(b + 3)(c + 3) = 3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":651.218605986,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":651.218609703,"data":"And I need to find the value of (a + 4)(b + 4)(c + 4). Hmm, interesting. Alright, let me think about how to approach this. Since the equations involve products of (a + n), (b + n), (c + n) for n = 1, 2, 3, and we need the next one for n = 4. Maybe there's a pattern or a recursive relation here?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":651.218615245,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":651.21861917,"data":"Let me denote P(n) = (a + n)(b + n)(c + n). Then the given equations are P(1) = 1, P(2) = 2, P(3) = 3, and we need to find P(4). So if I can find a way to express P(n) in terms of previous values, maybe I can find a formula for P(n) and then compute P(4).\n"}
